# Hybris display HAL SELinux policy
#
# Under droid-hal-init, vendor HAL processes (hwcomposer, display color, etc.)
# inherit the init domain because no exec-transition is configured for hybris.
# display.qservice is registered with the standard servicemanager (not
# vndservicemanager), so it gets the default_android_service label rather than
# vendor_qdisplay_service. Allow init to add and find it.
#
# default_android_service is a platform-public type; this rule is vendor-policy
# safe on sdm845 (shipped API 28, pre-strict-Treble).
#
# REMOVED: This rule violates two platform neverallows:
#   1. init.te:829  -> neverallow init service_manager_type:service_manager { add find };
#   2. domain.te:771 -> neverallow * default_android_service:service_manager *;
# These are hard security boundaries in Android — init must not register binder
# services, and no domain may use the generic default_android_service label.
#
# Because androidboot.selinux=permissive is already set, the display HAL will
# still function (AVCs are logged but not enforced). The proper long-term fix
# is to run the display HAL in its own domain (exec transition) and register
# the service with vndservicemanager so it gets a vendor-specific label.
#allow init default_android_service:service_manager { add find };
